updated_at: "2026-11-10T17:40:44.964Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Trusted reusable workflow jobs accept calendar annotations; steps retain strict semver; October action-pin release entry remains generated; behavioral reverts fail
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T16:19:16.938Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: reused PR #195 and fix/bot-green-1108. Remote head e0d816a; local merge 5a771dd already includes current main d67717d. Preserved the pending jobReference restriction and regression changes. Fetched all three unresolved threads with every comment; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. All three are valid. Historical item pm-slack-standup-6wvl retains October release provenance; this separate item owns the new calendar fix and review evidence. Never rewrite existing history."
  "2026-11-09T16:23:05.812Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in disposable copies: fixed pin suite passes 13/13. Removing only jobReference from packageWorkflow fails the job-only regression (12/13); removing only the calendar exception also fails it (12/13); restored fixed code passes 13/13. Both actual PR #191 and #192 workflow patches apply and pass 13/13. Self-review preserved unpadded strict-semver tags for steps; padded calendar annotations require job references. The provenance regression verifies separate item/title/release ownership. The October-entry regression remains pending the historical-state restoration decision."
  "2026-11-09T16:24:53.876Z",codex-agent,"Review round status: PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM60_GdG fixed by jobReference restriction with pin-policy regression; both behavior-only reverts fail 12/13 and fixed restoration passes 13/13. PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM60_GdA addressed by this distinct issue, preserved historical title/release, and removal of the calendar acceptance criterion from the October item; reverting only that criterion fails the new provenance test 0/1, fixed passes 1/1. PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM60_GdD is valid and remains blocked: the generator filters done statuses, and the inherited reopening removes the October entry. A prepared assertion reproduces the missing entry (0/1); restoring the historical closed state needs an exception to the explicit no-close rule, requested from the owner. Do not interpret this as an invalid finding or completed review round. That failing assertion is retained outside the committed test suite until the correction is authorized."
  "2026-11-09T16:24:54.652Z",codex-agent,"Validation: linked focused tests 14/14; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/identity-audit.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/sdk-adoption.test.ts passes 16/16; npm run accept:canonical-reader passes 1/1. npm run build, build:test, typecheck, lint, duplication (0 percent), docstring (140/140 declarations), verify:release-changelog-date, verify:release-publish-attestation, audit:prod (0 vulnerabilities), changelog:full, changelog:check and git diff --check pass. Committed dist rebuilt with no diff. Main history byte-prefix checks pass for both inherited changed streams; this new stream is append-only. pm health reports only existing global extension/host version-skew advisory, no merge reconciliation needed. Follow targeted-gates-only review scope: full release/coverage certification stays in CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/195/checks . Earlier local npm/Bun matrix timeouts remain tracked by pm-slack-standup-packed-timing; no new full-gate or coverage claim. No review threads were answered or resolved. Release this claim for orchestrator follow-up without closing it."
  "2026-11-09T21:09:57.976Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 (auto round 1) — all five findings fixed. Blocking provenance-tag duplication: removed gh:#191/#192 from the historical October item so each GitHub provenance tag stays on exactly one item (this one); the gated sync can publish issue updates again. Separate-release and October-entry findings: restored the historical item to its closed terminal state with the original close reason and completion timestamp; changelog:full regeneration restores the PR #131 entry under 2026.10.21 as the only changelog diff. Provenance test now asserts the closed status, the October entry under 2026.10.21, a class invariant that every closed non-duplicate item with a declared release matching a section keeps its entry there, and a class invariant that every gh: provenance tag is unique to one item. Owner-isolation finding: added a same-package case under another trusted owner (actions/pm-github/.github/workflows) to the calendar boundary test so removing the owner check fails the suite. Revert proofs in disposable copies: removing the unbraind owner condition fails the boundary test; restoring the duplicate tags fails the uniqueness test with both item ids; reopening the historical item fails the separate-provenance test; deleting the October entry fails the class test (pm-slack-standup-6wvl must stay listed under 2026.10.21). Before the fix the three provenance regressions failed 0/3 on the broken state; after the fix all pass."
  "2026-11-10T02:07:08.535Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3 (auto round 2) — one new finding, two stale threads verified. New tags-header finding: the provenance test now parses each item's tags header instead of matching whole-item text and asserts the calendar item carries exactly the #191, #192 and #195 provenance tags while the historical October item carries none, so a tag that leaves the header (or migrates to another item) fails the suite. Revert proofs in a disposable copy: deleting #195 from the calendar item's tags header fails the parsed-header assertion, and moving #195 to the historical item fails both the parsed-header assertion and the uniqueness test. Stale separate-release thread: already satisfied by the restored closed historical item with its October title and release plus the separate calendar item with no release yet; release notes for the calendar fix will describe it once the delivering release closes this item. Stale October-entry thread: the class test added last round asserts the entry under 2026.10.21 and the regenerated changelog restores it."
  "2026-11-10T17:27:11.545Z",codex-agent,"Final scoped continuation: preserved remote head 04d3d3b and merged origin/main at 8ba9a8d. Reused this PR item. The historical closure and both requested assertions already exist in 0f8e7d7 and 04d3d3b; verify their exact historical values and behavior rather than repeat or rewrite those mutations. Read every review thread with all comments and the latest CodeRabbit review; no outside-diff findings. No thread replies or resolutions will be posted. Run fresh disposable mutation proofs, focused tests, typecheck, lint, tracker/identity/changelog checks, and exactly one timeout-bounded npm test with two workers."
  "2026-11-10T17:29:10.123Z",codex-agent,"Fresh revert proofs (disposable tracked-file copy, node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/action-pin-provenance.test.ts): fixed baseline 3/3. Moving only the October entry into the November section while preserving its text elsewhere fails both the explicit October assertion and delivered-item invariant: 1/3 pass, 2 failures. Removing each of #191, #192 and #195 from only the tags header, while preserving all three exact strings in body text, independently fails the parsed-header assertion: 2/3 pass, 1 failure for each mutation. Reverting only the historical closed status fails 2/3. Restoring each fixture passes 3/3, and the final restored copy passes 3/3. No source tracker history was mutated for these proofs."
  "2026-11-10T17:29:12.298Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM60_GdA verification: pm history pm-slack-standup-6wvl --verify --strict-exit validates all 67 records; current item hash equals latest after_hash. Compared original October close event with restored close event and current item: identical original close_reason, status closed and completed_at 2026-10-21T18:48:09.851Z. Release matches the original assignment 2026.10.21; title describes the original PR #131 delivery. Calendar work remains on this separate in-progress item with exactly #191/#192/#195 tags and no October release. Existing changed history streams retain main as a byte-identical prefix. Preserved the already-correct restoration without another close event; closed no other item. changelog:full preserves the original October entry. CodeRabbit chat-limit response is missing verification, not approval."
  "2026-11-10T17:29:59.874Z",codex-agent,"Focused restored tests pass 16/16 (provenance 3, workflow pin policy 13), including pm test --run --only-last --progress. Identity/release/SDK targeted tests pass 16/16. Typecheck, build:test, lint, duplication (0 percent across 70 sources), docstrings (140 declarations), release-date and publish-attestation checks pass. Full npm test is running exactly once under timeout 2700, using the package script node --test --test-concurrency=2. Strict tracker health reports one gate-failing local advisory: pm-github extension host/runtime version skew (pinned host 2026.11.7 versus local extension 2026.11.10). History integrity and drift checks pass; two unrelated stale items and inherited provenance-domain advisories remain. No thresholds or unrelated tracker items changed."
  "2026-11-10T17:40:44.229Z",codex-agent,"Final full-suite receipt: timeout 2700 npm test ran exactly once, completed within the budget in 696901 ms, and exited 1. Read the final parent summary: 363 tests, 361 pass, 2 fail, 0 cancelled, 0 skipped, 0 todo. Both failures are the existing test/accept-packed.test.ts npm/Bun matrices with npm_execpath inherited/unset reaching their unchanged 290000 ms parent limits (290537 ms and 290522 ms observed). No full-suite success or coverage claim; CI must certify the full gate. This is the recurrence already tracked by pm-slack-standup-packed-timing; no duplicate item or timeout/threshold change. Canonical-reader acceptance passes 1/1; changelog:full and changelog:check pass with the historical entry under 2026.10.21; build leaves committed dist unchanged. Final focused, history verification, changelog and identity checks will run after the last tracker write. Release only this claim and leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
